{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q1592091","formula":"KNaMg₂(PO₄)₂*14H₂O","hill":"H28KMg2NaO22P2","elements":["H","O","Na","Mg","P","K"],"composition":{"H":28.0,"K":1.0,"O":22.0,"P":2.0,"Mg":2.0,"Na":1.0},"names":{"en":"Hazenite","ru":"Хазенит"},"descriptions":{"en":"Hazenite is a hydrous phosphate mineral with chemical formula of KNaMg2(PO4)2 · 14 H2O, therefore a hydrous alkali magnesium phosphate. It is a member of the struvite group. It was first described for an occurrence adjacent to Mono Lake, California, and named after Robert M. Hazen of the Carnegie Institute.","ru":"Хазенит (англ. Hazenite) — водный фосфат K, Na и Mg из группы струвита. Химическая формула — KNaMg2(PO4)2·14H2O. Имеет вид радиальных срастаний из удлинённо-таблитчатых или призматических кристаллов или одиночных пластинчатых кристаллов размером до 0,06×0,12×0,40 мм."},"fame":7,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1592091","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hazenite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A5%D0%B0%D0%B7%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%B8%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"similar":[{"id":"Q420287","formula":"Ca₆Al₂(SO₄)₃(OH)₁₂·26H₂O","names":{"en":"Ettringite","ru":"Эттрингит","uk":"Етрингіт"},"elements":["H","O","Al","S","Ca"],"fame":21,"kind":null},{"id":"Q2706126","formula":"Ca₃Si(OH)₆(SO₄)(CO₃)·12H₂O","names":{"en":"Thaumasite"},"elements":["H","C","O","Si","S","Ca"],"fame":14,"kind":"crystal"},{"id":"Q2896152","formula":"Ca₆Cr₂(SO₄)₃(OH)₁₂·26H₂O","names":{"en":"Bentorite","uk":"Бенторит"},"elements":["H","O","S","Ca","Cr"],"fame":14,"kind":null},{"id":"Q3643